+
+## Turn usage (issue #93)
+
+The chosen contract keeps one summed usage argument, preserving the common consumer shape. A per-round breakdown is rejected because provider-call granularity is not needed for turn billing and would widen the public surface.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per completed user message and receives the sum of `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` across every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer; rounds without usage contribute nothing, all-missing usage stays undefined, and a no-tool turn retains its existing usage ([validated by: reports the sum of every provider call once per turn, preserving missing usage and direct answers](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator-usage.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+- When both a running total and a round's usage are defined, `accumulateUsage` returns their field-wise sum ([validated by: returns the field-wise sum of two defined values](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L26)).
+- When the running total is absent and a round reports usage, `accumulateUsage` returns that usage as the new total ([validated by: returns the defined value when the accumulator is absent](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L18)).
+- When a round reports no usage, `accumulateUsage` returns the running total unchanged ([validated by: returns the accumulator when the next value is absent](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L22)).
+- When both values are absent, `accumulateUsage` returns `undefined` ([validated by: returns undefined when both are absent](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L14)).
+- `accumulateUsage` does not mutate the running total it receives ([validated by: does not mutate the accumulator input](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L30)).
+- `accumulateUsage` does not mutate the new-value input it receives ([validated by: does not mutate the next-value input](../../src/orchestration/orchestratorHelpers.test.ts#L36)).
+
+The public hook signature must explicitly name its usage as a turn total. Release this behaviour change with a MINOR version bump and a changelog entry explaining that existing consumers now record larger totals for tool-heavy turns.
